In article <1993Sep10.103226.19702@waikato.ac.nz>, drysdall@waikato.ac.nz writes:
>What about this:
>Running away from some critters, then I remember I have a wand. Haven't
>identified it, but I know that I engraved with it. What was the message? I
>think it was "The bugs on the ground speed up" so I zap myself with it.
>Result: It was a wand of striking and I kill myself (the wand of speed was in
>the LAST game, not this one). The high-scores only said "Killed by a wand" so I
>was a bit disappointed with this bit.
>The consequences of playing too many games in a row...

Immediately after you engrave with a wand you should ALWAYS name it.
Even if you couldn't figure out what it was.  A while into the game,
I often end up with wands named:

"bugs stop moving" since I don't know if it's death or sleep.
"eng vanishes" since it could be make invisible, or teleport, or
                cancellation
"no eng effect" could be any number of things (including any wand with no
                 charges).

Then if I get caught in a dangerous situation like you, I would zap the
monsters with the wand called "bugs stop moving", and find out which one 
it is.

One the other hand, if you get a message like "the bugs speed up", I'd zap
myself with it right away to identify it.
